SM(211,{"n":"1 Timothy 1","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Timothy 1.mp3","d":2410.5,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study holy scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Council of God."],[8.16,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.72,"So we'll go ahead and get started."],[22.88,"And when we get started in just a moment, and it really will be this time, just a moment."],[32.64,"Last time all we did was the introduction to First Timothy."],[36.4,"So I'm not going to re-introduce the introduction."],[41.28,"By the time people are hearing this recording, that'll be that recording will be available."],[47.44,"The one thing I didn't go over in that introduction is I didn't say much about Saint Timothy himself, to whom St."],[55.2,"Paul is addressing this letter."],[59.76,"But most of what we know about St."],[62.0,"Timothy, frankly, we know from these two letters."],[65.52,"So we'll be sort of talking about that as we go along."],[71.76,"Uh through first and second uh Timothy."],[75.52,"Um so um but we have super brief."],[80.72,"This is unlike the epistles we've been reading so far."],[84.32,"This is a letter that St."],[86.0,"Paul wrote to St."],[87.12,"Timothy, so it's to a particular person rather than going to a church or to a group of churches."],[92.72,"So it's a slightly different format."],[95.52,"He speaks slightly differently and about slightly different topics."],[100.0,"Obviously, St. Timothy is not only an individual person and not a church, but he's someone who's worked closely with Saint Paul and who has a leadership position in these early Christian communities, and who, by way of this letter, he is uh sending to fulfill a specific role in church leadership."],[121.48,"So the topics he's going to talk about rather than dealing with the kind of topics we've seen in previous epistles where he's talking about things going on in particular churches and clarifying uh theological issues and addressing practical issues."],[136.84,"Um he's sort of here in a sort of mentoring role with Saint Timothy, and so is going to be talking to him in terms of as a fellow leader."],[147.64,"Here are things you need to keep in mind and and look out for, etc."],[152.84,"Uh so with that brief uh introduction, unless anybody has any leftover uh comments or questions or good jokes they heard on the bus on the way here."],[168.52,"Uh, we'll go ahead and uh uh start with Saint Paul's first epistle to Timothy chapter one, verse one."],[179.72,"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ, by the commandment of God our Savior, and the Lord Jesus Christ our hope."],[188.36,"So this is fairly typical by now."],[191.4,"We see as how St."],[192.92,"Paul, you know, there's there are a certain number of elements in these epistles that are just qualities of how you do a formal letter, right, in the first century."],[202.28,"Um this is one of you begin with, you know, your name."],[208.04,"That's sort of the opposite of how we do in English."],[211.0,"In English, you begin with the address E."],[215.4,"And then at the bottom you sign your name."],[217.88,"Um so uh, as we've seen, Paul introduces himself first in all of these."],[226.24,"And here he's particularly identifying himself as an apostle of Jesus Christ."],[233.36,"We've talked about how apostle means someone who's sent."],[237.68,"And St. Paul tends to, in the particular ways in which he introduces himself, even here."],[244.64,"We've talked about how at the beginning of his epistles, St."],[247.28,"Paul always sort of lays out some of the themes that he's going to develop later on."],[251.52,"And he even seeds some of that into the way he introduces himself and that kind of thing."],[256.48,"This is one of them."],[257.52,"So he's identifying himself as someone sent by Jesus Christ on a mission."],[262.08,"This epistle, he's going to be sending Saint Timothy on a mission."],[267.76,"So that's part of why he mentions that here."],[272.4,"Because of course, St."],[273.52,"Timothy knows who Saint Paul is."],[276.0,"Like he doesn't have to explain the things he's pointing out, he's pointing out with a reason."],[285.36,"That was by the commandment of God our Savior and the Lord Jesus Christ, our hope."],[293.52,"So we've seen he often has God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ as this sort of doublet or pairing."],[301.84,"Here it's God our Savior and Jesus Christ our hope."],[309.44,"So this is something he's going to be developing as we go forward."],[317.12,"I don't want to say too much about it now, but the idea of uh the ideas of salvation and then future hope are ideas he's going to be developing."],[328.88,"And there's also a little bit of a uh notice here that he says an apostle of Jesus Christ by the commandment of God our Savior and the Lord Jesus Christ."],[338.12,"So he goes from Christ to God the Father back to back to Christ."],[343.32,"Because of course, they're as we've talked before, we've touched on uh the Holy Trinity, they act as one."],[352.12,"Three persons have one activity, one will and one activity."],[355.64,"Um they act together in uh sending Saint Paul."],[360.92,"Verse 2 to Timothy, a true son in the faith, grace, mercy, and peace from God our Father and Jesus Christ our Lord."],[369.4,"Right. And so we've seen him use variations on that introduction."],[374.6,"He's got that couplet again that he usually uses."],[378.92,"And uh this is sort of the equivalent of our dear."],[384.6,"In terms of the addressee."],[386.36,"Notice also that he refers to Timothy as a true son uh in the faith."],[391.72,"Um I always point these out uh that Saint Paul fairly consistently and continuously, as we've seen, refers to himself as a father to not just someone like St."],[405.8,"Timothy, who he mentors, but to the people in his churches."],[410.68,"Um the reason I always point that out is our Protestant friends don't like that language."],[418.76,"Um but this is language that St."],[421.88,"Paul uses all the time."],[423.8,"Uh so unless you want to say that St."],[426.2,"Paul is fairly consistently uh violating what Christ said in the Call No Man Father passage, then you we might need to understand what Christ said in a different way."],[434.84,"So St. Right."],[441.52,"Paul consistently uses this kind of father-son terminology or father-children terminology to describe a relationship between them as humans."],[453.36,"So when Christ says, call no man father, it's in a litany of titles."],[460.4,"Call no man father because you have one father who's in heaven."],[462.96,"Call no man teacher because you have one teacher."],[466.32,"And it's in the context of him talking telling his disciples, you're not to try to get titles for yourself and authority and lord it over the people who you're teaching."],[480.24,"Because that's how the rulers of the Gentiles do it."],[483.2,"They lord it over one another."],[485.52,"That's not how the disciples are to lead."],[488.08,"So that's what he's talking about."],[490.0,"That's what Christ is talking about when he addresses that."],[493.12,"He's addressing the kind of titles that the Pharisees would want to have."],[497.6,"That rabbis would want to have."],[500.16,"The title teacher, of course, is rabbi."],[502.96,"You're not to use these."],[504.8,"Um when Saint Paul, as I said, uses this language, he's using it to describe the relationship between himself and particular people."],[518.32,"So he's not coming to someone and demanding that they call him by a certain title."],[525.44,"Out of his ego or something."],[527.84,"Right? So when he says, St."],[529.52,"Timothy is a true son, there is nothing in that."],[533.44,"He's saying you're like a son to me, right, in the faith."],[537.44,"There's no element of that where he's trying to assert domination or control over Saint Timothy, or where St."],[539.84,"Timothy would have received it that way."],[545.48,"Right? It's a term of affection."],[547.64,"It's it's the opposite."],[550.68,"Um, and the same kind of thing when he uses that language addressing churches."],[556.12,"Right? When he says he's he's a father to them, he means he loves them and he's trying to guide them to maturity."],[563.32,"Which is what a father does."],[565.72,"Um he's not saying, I'm the boss and you're all gonna lick my boots."],[571.48,"That's quite the opposite."],[575.56,"Verse three, as I urged you when I went into Macedonia, remain in Ephesus, that you may charge some that they teach no other doctrine, nor give heed to fables and endless genealogies, which cause disputes rather than godly edification, which is in faith."],[592.2,"Now the purpose of the commandment is love from a pure heart, from a good conscience, and from sincere faith."],[601.64,"So um we've seen before, we've seen St."],[607.16,"Timothy get mentioned in several of St."],[609.48,"Paul's epistles, we've already read."],[611.48,"And a lot of the times when he's mentioned, it's because Saint Paul wanted to go visit a church and he couldn't for whatever reason."],[618.12,"He was imprisoned, or just he couldn't get away from where he was, or it was too far away."],[622.44,"And so he would send Saint Timothy there, sort of as his representative, you know, and then St."],[627.96,"Timothy would come back to St."],[629.24,"Paul and give him some kind of report about what's going on there."],[632.68,"Um, and what issues, if any, right, there were that needed to be addressed."],[638.2,"And so we see that that's as St."],[640.52,"Paul writes this letter to St."],[642.12,"Timothy, there is a similar sort of situation going on."],[648.0,"Because he has sent St."],[650.08,"Timothy clearly to Ephesus."],[651.68,"We we've talked about how Ephesus itself was sort of the major home base for the Christian movement in the first couple centuries."],[665.04,"I hope they don't hear this at the Archdiocese, because I know we all want to say it was Antioch, but really it was kind of Ephesus for the first few centuries."],[675.68,"And not just because St."],[676.96,"Paul ministered there, but of course Saint John went there, St."],[681.12,"Mary Magdalene went there, uh the Theotokos was there for a while."],[685.36,"Uh this was just a major hub."],[687.6,"And it was a major hub city in the Roman world, as we talked about when we read St."],[691.36,"Paul's Epistle to the Ephesians, terms of shipping and commerce and everything."],[695.04,"It was on a main road."],[696.32,"There were reasons why it sort of became the central city in uh in early Christianity."],[703.92,"So he's he sent Saint Timothy there, and uh he wants Saint Timothy to stay there for a little bit because apparently there are some issues going on that he wants Saint Timothy to help resolve."],[719.04,"Um that being based on this that uh there's some people with some differences of opinion about matters of theology."],[730.16,"And these are differences of opinion that St."],[732.88,"Paul clearly thinks are mostly unimportant."],[737.16,"Right? Because he's not telling them, you know, hey, this belief is a heresy, you need to throw these people out of the church, or you need to correct these people who say this."],[747.16,"Right? Instead, he says, tell them not to listen to fables and endless genealogies."],[754.2,"Meaning these are these are the minutiae."],[757.4,"That everybody argues about."],[759.56,"We still have this today."],[761.56,"And he's saying this becomes a problem, even though these things in and of themselves aren't hugely important."],[767.8,"If they start developing into rifts in the community, where people are separating from each other and forming factions and arguing and debating, and it splits up the unity of the church, then that becomes a major issue."],[781.88,"Yes, sir. What about genealogies?"],[788.28,"Right. So the genealogies we're talking about here are not just."],[794.12,"We think of genealogies purely in terms of like ancestry.com."],[799.0,"Uh, where going and finding who's descended from from whom, and since there's a lot of pagan converts, why would that matter?"],[807.88,"Right. Um, this is referring more to a type of genealogy within the the uh religious world."],[817.64,"Like Hesiod's theogony."],[821.24,"Um sort of systems, systems of thought, uh, rankings of angels, uh, systems of doctrine, um, detailed explanations of the planets and the stars and constellations and things."],[839.32,"Um, and this, of course, this happened."],[842.24,"We're kind of aware that, okay, yeah, that kind of thing was big with the the pagans."],[847.24,"And that they might try to apply it to Christianity."],[849.56,"That was also really big within first century forms of Judaism."],[853.56,"Uh, there's lots of astrology, there was lots of that kind of thing."],[858.88,"And so this is the kind of thing he's talking about."],[863.12,"Right. People trying to develop these sort of elaborate systems and sis systems of symbolism of different things and interpretations of allegorical interpretations of scriptural passages, you know, and right."],[878.88,"That's the kind of thing he's talking about."],[881.2,"And then sitting and fighting and arguing about those."],[885.36,"Right, yeah. Yeah."],[886.96,"Yeah. It's not who's descended from who in terms of humans."],[890.32,"Yeah. Yeah. Taxonomies might be a better translation, actually."],[896.64,"Although even that isn't quite, but um."],[902.32,"Right. And so he says these just cause disputes."],[906.4,"Nobody nobody advances in the faith."],[908.88,"Nobody has ever become more pious or more virtuous based on arguing about this kind of stuff."],[915.52,"Right. I've said before I've never had anyone show up at the church and say, I really need to become a Christian because I lost this argument on the internet."],[926.16,"And I just don't know what to do now."],[928.88,"Right. Like that that doesn't happen."],[931.2,"So he's saying you need to get them to sort of knock this stuff off."],[935.44,"Right. Um, that this isn't important."],[938.96,"And that's why he says now the purpose of the commandment is love from a pure heart, a good conscience, and sincere faith, which again, we've, as we've said before, should be more like faithfulness."],[954.24,"But this is what we're after."],[957.12,"Because love that comes from a pure heart and a good conscience and sincere faithfulness or sincere loyalty."],[959.84,"That is what brings the community together."],[964.12,"That is what builds people up."],[967.4,"That is what brings people closer to Christ."],[969.96,"So this is what we're looking for, not arguing about this dumb stuff that doesn't matter and who's right and who's smartest and who knows the most."],[979.72,"But this kind of love for each other."],[987.88,"Verse 6, from which some."],[998.44,"Yeah, layout fail."],[1000.36,"Um from which some, having strayed, have turned aside to idle talk, desiring to be teachers of the law, understanding neither what they say nor the things which they affirm."],[1013.16,"Um so they've strayed from that kind of love."],[1019.16,"Some people in the community have strayed from that kind of love."],[1022.68,"Um, and so now they're into the idle talk because they want to set themselves up as teachers."],[1029.56,"They want to be the one, I'm the one who's in the know and I can explain all this to you."],[1033.72,"Um, again, this is a problem we still have."],[1036.92,"Uh if anything, social media has made this far worse on the internet, because anyone who wants good too can just decide I'm going to be a teacher now, uh, and start trying to develop a following and start um saying whatever they want to say."],[1053.24,"And St. Paul, who uh, if anybody had has the qualifications to be a teacher of the law, it's St."],[1060.6,"Paul. Is saying they don't even know what they're talking about."],[1064.04,"Like they're wanting to argue about all this stuff."],[1064.52,"Right. They don't even really get it themselves."],[1070.4,"They're just trying to make themselves look smart."],[1073.76,"And set themselves up above other people."],[1079.92,"Verse 8, but we know that the law is good if one uses it lawfully."],[1087.04,"Which is kind of a tautology."],[1092.96,"If you use the law in accordance with the law, it's the law."],[1096.56,"Yeah. Um, remember also what's being translated here as law is Torah, really."],[1104.8,"Right. So he's he's not just talking about like moral commandments."],[1110.88,"He's talking about the Torah, right, the revelation of God."],[1115.68,"So these people aren't just teaching about moral do's and don'ts."],[1120.96,"This is a larger scale thing."],[1125.12,"And so uh he's saying that when when you another way to rephrase this might be when you teach the Torah on its own terms, when you're teaching what the scriptures actually say, that's good."],[1142.24,"That's good. Uh verse 9, knowing this, that the law is not made for a righteous person, but for the lawless and insubordinate, for ungodly and for sinners, for unholy and profane, I'm leaving out the italicized added words, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers, for fornicators, for sodomites, for kidnappers, for liars, for perjurers."],[1171.88,"And if there is any other thing that is contrary to sound doctrine, according to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust."],[1182.44,"So a couple of interesting things here."],[1186.12,"So he's saying the uh the the law, the Torah is good, but it's aimed at the people who need it."],[1198.44,"It's aimed at the the people who need it."],[1201.96,"Meaning, if someone is uh, if someone is already in the the church community."],[1214.12,"And if someone is living as a Christian and seeking to follow Christ, okay, then what's important are those things he just laid out."],[1224.28,"That love, that faithfulness, that loyalty."],[1229.0,"And he's saying it's a good thing to go and teach the Torah to people."],[1235.64,"But that's directed to the people in Ephesus who aren't in the community, many of whom he lists there."],[1245.08,"And some of these are a little euphemistic, some of them are, some of them are fairly direct, but some of the like kidnappers, you're like, well, how many kidnappers were there?"],[1255.48,"Like were people just running around kidnapping people."],[1258.2,"Um, so some of these are euphobism."],[1259.96,"But anyway, he gives this litany of sort of sins, the wicked, and he's referring to people outside the church."],[1268.24,"Right? So, yes, you need to be going to them, right, and teaching them."],[1273.44,"Who is you in this case?"],[1275.44,"He's not, no, he's not talking to St."],[1277.12,"Timothy. These people, he's saying, these people who want to set themselves up as teachers."],[1282.96,"You want to set yourself up as a teacher of the law."],[1285.92,"Don't set yourself up inside the Christian community."],[1288.72,"Why don't you go outside?"],[1290.88,"To the people who don't know who Christ is."],[1295.12,"And teach them about God."],[1299.6,"Right? Rather than sitting here trying to set yourself up as a teacher inside the community and causing all these riffs and divisions and arguments and right."],[1309.84,"And that's why he says."],[1314.4,"Right? He says, if there's any other thing that's contrary to sound doctrine, we tend to separate, like, there's like doctrine, and then there's morality."],[1325.28,"Right? So we say doctrine is stuff like about the Holy Trinity or about the two natures of Christ."],[1332.16,"This is doctrine."],[1333.36,"And then you also have this moral stuff, and if you're a Christian, you have to follow the moral stuff."],[1337.2,"For St. Paul, the problem with all these behaviors is they're against doctrine."],[1342.72,"So there's not this disconnect."],[1345.28,"The Torah is both."],[1347.04,"It's both who God is, who Christ is, and the commandments."],[1351.76,"You can't separate the two."],[1353.92,"So he calls both of them doctrine, and then he says, according to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, so the gospel also includes both."],[1363.84,"Right? The gospel also includes both."],[1366.56,"Right. So if these people want to preach, and these people want to teach, they need to go out and preach and teach the people who are outside the church to try to bring them to Christ and bring them into the church."],[1378.88,"Right? Essentially, if you want to be a leader, go be a leader."],[1383.72,"Right? Don't come and try and take over the house of God."],[1389.4,"And make it your house."],[1390.92,"But go out and, you know, bring people into the house of God."],[1398.44,"Right? So that's what he's getting at there."],[1402.68,"And again, it's not saying Timothy, you need to throw these people out."],[1406.68,"You need to excommunicate them, they're no good."],[1410.68,"It's these people are misguided."],[1414.36,"Right? And if they have if they actually have any qualifications for this task, they need to go do the task."],[1421.32,"Right? In the correct, in the correct place to the correct audience."],[1428.6,"Verse 12. And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord who has enabled me because he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry."],[1438.6,"Although I was formerly a blasphemer, a persecutor, and an insolent man, but I obtained mercy because I did it ignorantly in unbelief."],[1449.8,"So he's comparing these people to himself."],[1458.76,"Right. Right? Why?"],[1475.16,"Ignorantly. I didn't know."],[1479.08,"He didn't know Christ."],[1480.04,"He didn't really know God."],[1481.24,"He thought he did, but he didn't really."],[1483.8,"Right. But God counted him faithful and brought him into the ministry."],[1490.16,"Right. And that can happen for these people too."],[1492.8,"Right? Right now they're ignorant and they're, you know, they're doing this causing these problems."],[1498.16,"But they can also, we can, we can, say, Timothy, we can redirect them."],[1503.84,"We can redirect their energies to help the ministry of the Lord."],[1515.36,"Verse 14, and the grace of our Lord was exceedingly abundant, with faith and love, which are in Christ Jesus."],[1524.64,"This is a faithful saying and worthy of all acceptance, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am chief."],[1535.2,"Okay. So you may recognize that from the prayer we pray before receiving communion."],[1542.08,"And when we pray it, we're referring to ourselves, just to make it clear."],[1545.84,"It's not Christ came to the world to save sinners, of whom St."],[1549.44,"Paul is chief."],[1552.08,"And when we pray that before communion, we ought to actually mean it."],[1557.52,"That's one of those things it's easy to say but hard to mean."],[1560.4,"Because somewhere in the back of our head, we're saying, of whom, well, actually, I know this guy who's probably the chief, but I'm pretty bad too."],[1569.04,"Right? That's not the point."],[1573.68,"Right? That's not the point."],[1575.6,"And that's not the point St."],[1576.72,"Paul's making here."],[1577.6,"Right. St. Paul is making the point that."],[1581.76,"If he can save me, meaning St."],[1584.16,"Paul, he can save these people too."],[1588.24,"Right? I'm as bad as it gets."],[1589.84,"So that means Christ's mercy is available to everybody, if it's available to me."],[1596.2,"Right? Because if there was anyone who couldn't find salvation, right, then I'm in deep trouble."],[1604.76,"The only way I'm in is if it's possible for everyone."],[1615.4,"Verse 16. However, for this reason I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might show all long suffering as a pattern to those who are going to believe on him for everlasting life."],[1627.4,"Now to the king, eternal, immortal, invisible, to God who alone is wise, be honor and glory forever and ever."],[1633.96,"Amen. So he's saying, see, I'm what happened with St."],[1639.8,"Paul is a pattern."],[1642.44,"Right. And so that pattern can be applied to these other people too."],[1647.08,"Right? These other people can find salvation potentially in the same way."],[1663.88,"Verse 18, this charge I commit to you, son Timothy, according to the prophecies previously made concerning you, that by them you may wage the good warfare."],[1676.04,"Why couldn't they just say fight the good fight?"],[1679.08,"Well you gotta second guess the anyway."],[1682.84,"Having having faith in a good conscience, which some have rejected, concerning the faith, have suffered shipwreck."],[1690.84,"Of whom are Hymenaus and Alexander, whom I delivered to Satan that they may learn not to blaspheme."],[1703.36,"We'll get there."],[1706.64,"Right. So he starts with uh right, he says, I'm charging you with this."],[1715.84,"Um, because of the prophecies made concerning him."],[1718.88,"Now, this isn't sort of weird predictions."],[1721.36,"This is not like at his birth there were signs in the sky, and the oracle said, Saint Timothy will go."],[1727.68,"Um we talked about this back when we were in uh 1 Corinthians, that uh prophecy is speaking and revealing the things of God to people."],[1743.12,"So Moses is the first and main prophet of the Old Testament."],[1746.48,"He's sort of the paradigm of the Old Testament."],[1748.96,"There are a couple of places where he predicts things that are gonna happen in the future, but that's like.1% of what Moses said was predicting the future."],[1761.04,"Even though that's how we think of prophecy now."],[1764.32,"Most of what he was doing was teaching the people."],[1769.92,"And preaching to them."],[1771.04,"The book of Deuteronomy is essentially a long sermon by Moses to the people of Israel before they go into the into the land of Canaan."],[1780.24,"And what we see, you know, when when the prophet Nathan comes and confronts David, he's not predicting the future, he's telling them about the past, about something David had just done."],[1790.68,"Right. And and convicting him about it."],[1793.84,"Or you look at Prophets Isaiah, Jeremiah, Ezekiel."],[1797.36,"They come to the people and convict them of their sin."],[1801.0,"So the line between prophecy and what we call preaching is a very slender one and in some cases non-existent."],[1809.08,"Right. So this is St."],[1811.16,"Paul saying, You've heard me say all these things."],[1816.36,"You've heard, and I commissioned you to do this."],[1818.68,"You've heard other leaders, other apostles."],[1821.64,"We've all commissioned you to do this."],[1824.36,"And so you need to keep acting, right, in terms of that, in terms of what has been preached for you and proclaimed for you to do."],[1836.04,"So that you may wage the good warfare or fight the good fight."],[1839.56,"Um that being spiritual warfare, not going pick fights."],[1844.68,"He just said the opposite of go and pick fights in the church."],[1849.0,"Um faithfulness and a good conscience, which some have rejected, and concerning the faithless have suffered shipwreck."],[1859.0,"So there are some people who have rejected the things that were spoken to you."],[1866.04,"Meaning they weren't just spoken to or about Saint Timothy."],[1871.0,"There are other people who have rejected that preaching and that teaching."],[1874.92,"He names a couple of them here."],[1877.32,"And because they rejected that, what happened?"],[1880.04,"They suffered shipwreck."],[1881.32,"So what's the imagery that he's using?"],[1884.52,"Right? There's a course."],[1885.88,"You're out at sea, you've got a course."],[1887.88,"You stray off that course, you're gonna get in trouble."],[1891.32,"In a thousand different ways."],[1893.12,"Right. So he's comparing the preaching that St."],[1896.76,"Timothy has received and that these other people received to this course, right, to navigate."],[1902.52,"Usually we've seen sort of way in road language."],[1904.92,"And so he's saying they have rejected it."],[1906.24,"This is more sea lane language."],[1911.92,"They ignored the course instructions, and now they're shipwrecked."],[1917.6,"Right? Now notice shipwrecked."],[1920.08,"Not now they're terrible people."],[1922.24,"Not now we hate them."],[1924.24,"Right? No, now they're shipwrecked, they're in trouble."],[1927.44,"St. Paul was shipwrecked twice, remember?"],[1929.44,"They're in trouble out on the sea."],[1932.32,"They need help."],[1934.08,"Right. And then he gives the example of these two people, whom he delivered to Satan."],[1940.4,"So they would learn not to blaspheme."],[1941.84,"And he's used this language before."],[1943.2,"We saw this in 1 Corinthians, remember?"],[1945.6,"He talked about handing someone over to Satan for the destruction of their flesh that their soul might be saved."],[1952.08,"That's even more kind of drastic than this."],[1955.52,"But what's what's the idea here?"],[1959.36,"The demonic powers, as we've talked about before."],[1963.68,"That answer the question why does God let them roam around the world causing trouble?"],[1969.92,"Right? Trying to destroy humans."],[1978.24,"Paul is appealing to here is that sort of inadvertently they end up doing God's will."],[1987.52,"So they want evil."],[1989.44,"They want to destroy humans, but God uses them by testing and trying people to bring people to repentance."],[2000.24,"Right? To bring them to faith."],[2003.84,"Sort of against their wills."],[2006.0,"And begrudgingly, they sort of end up end up serving him."],[2009.52,"And this is the same idea."],[2011.24,"So he hands them over to Satan, not so that they would go to hell."],[2014.92,"Right? He hands them over to Satan so they will learn not to blaspheme."],[2020.68,"Right. So when uh, and this is important because this is paradigmatic for understanding a lot of the Old Testament and a fair amount of the New Testament."],[2033.4,"When we read about God's wrath and about God punishing, right, what we're really talking about is God no longer protecting his people or specific people from the consequences of their actions."],[2050.84,"So the only reason Satan doesn't have everyone is because God is stopping him from having them."],[2059.56,"Right? If I get into a fight with Satan, if I get into a fight with the devil, I lose if it's just me."],[2066.92,"Every time he's like a vast cosmic intelligence, I'm a dude."],[2072.44,"So that's not even an even match."],[2084.92,"As St. Paul says elsewhere, God disciplines every son whom he loves."],[2090.52,"Why do you discipline a child."],[2093.32,"If you're a parent, not because you hate them."],[2096.04,"Hopefully, not because you're angry with them and want to beat them."],[2099.4,"Unfortunately, some human parents do that."],[2102.36,"But God's not like them."],[2104.16,"Right? You do it to try to get them back in line, to try to teach them something, to try and keep them from something worse."],[2111.4,"Right? So if you tell your kid not to play in the street and you catch him playing in the street, and you swat him a few times on the rear end."],[2120.64,"Your goal is to keep him from playing in the street so he doesn't get hit by a truck."],[2125.04,"Not that just like you like beating him or you made up an arbitrary rule."],[2129.68,"Right? And so this is the same idea here that St."],[2133.2,"Paul's appealing to."],[2135.6,"Right? Heading over to Satan means we excommunicate him."],[2138.56,"He's outside the community now."],[2141.2,"He's outside the church."],[2143.2,"He's in that area of the world that's still under the control of Satan."],[2147.2,"That's not going to be good for him."],[2149.52,"That's not going to be fun for him."],[2151.68,"This is not going to be a good experience."],[2154.24,"Right? And so the hope is that from that he will repent."],[2161.84,"He'll learn. Right?"],[2163.6,"He'll say, hey, I need to get back in."],[2168.08,"I need to repent."],[2169.12,"I need to do what's right."],[2170.24,"I need to fix what I broke."],[2172.72,"Right? That's that's the goal."],[2175.84,"Right? But sometimes, in order to get someone to that point where they'll repent, right, you have to let the leash go a little."],[2184.48,"Right? You have to let them experience a little bit."],[2187.36,"Right? If you have a child, and throughout that child's life, you stop them from ever experiencing the consequences of their actions."],[2197.52,"Anytime there's going to be a negative consequence from something that for something they've done, you shield them from it."],[2203.52,"That child will very quickly become a monster."],[2208.24,"Rather literally. Right?"],[2210.6,"They'll become a completely immoral narcissistic monster if they never experience any of the consequences of their actions."],[2217.8,"Right? And so, if you're a parent who loves your child and wants your child to grow into an adult who's a human and not a monster, then sometimes you're gonna have to let them experience at least a little of the consequences."],[2231.56,"Now you don't let them go play in the street and get hit by the truck."],[2235.24,"Right? But sometimes you let them, you know, they have to go work to earn the money to pay for the window they broke."],[2243.24,"They have to learn, you know, and this is the same idea."],[2249.08,"So there's no desire for these people to be tormented by Satan."],[2254.04,"But if it's gotten to the point that that's the only thing you think might bring them to repentance, then you need to let that happen to try to bring them to repentance."],[2265.56,"So through this whole chapter, St."],[2269.48,"Paul is talking to St."],[2270.68,"Timothy about what?"],[2272.52,"About all the troublemakers in the church in Ephesus."],[2277.64,"A couple of really serious troublemakers who have been excommunicated who have been kicked out, and then a whole bunch of lower grade troublemakers, right, who are active in the community."],[2286.44,"And he's talking to him as a fellow leader."],[2289.24,"How do you handle the troublemakers in this community?"],[2293.32,"How do you handle the people who today have decided to be problem children?"],[2297.8,"And it may not be the same people every day."],[2299.72,"Some of these people may get their act together and somebody else may start causing trouble."],[2304.84,"But how do you handle them?"],[2306.04,"And what we see is the through line through this whole first chapter is what?"],[2309.32,"St. Paul is concerned about their coming to Christ."],[2314.04,"Right? What he wants is their repentance."],[2316.92,"So if they're low grade troublemakers, it's how do we redirect this and use it for the gospel of Christ?"],[2324.8,"How do we get them back on board with the program?"],[2328.24,"And if it's gone a long way like these two folks who he mentions, then it's well, what do we this is a bad situation."],[2337.52,"They're apparently blaspheming."],[2340.32,"And St. Paul says he was a blasphemer before his conversion."],[2343.6,"He just said that a few verses earlier."],[2345.76,"So there's hope for them too, but we need to take sort of more drastic action with them to try to get them to repent and come back."],[2354.56,"But every group of people who he describes."],[2357.76,"The low grade troublemakers, these two have been excommunicated, even the pagans in Ephesus who are outside the community, St."],[2364.64,"Paul wants all of them to come to know Christ and come to salvation."],[2368.8,"That's the goal."],[2370.8,"How do we go about it?"],[2372.48,"That's what he's strategizing with St."],[2374.24,"Timothy as sort of his protege."],[2376.4,"As mentor to father to son, mentor to protege."],[2380.08,"How here's how to sort of game this out and figure out what kind of approach you need to take with these different people, but the goal's the same."],[2388.08,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the whole council of God."],[2395.44,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2400.8,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":32.64,"lv":2,"h":"Recap and who Timothy is","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Last time: only the <b>introduction to 1 Timothy</b> - not re-introducing</li><li class=\"d0\">Not covered: <b>St. Timothy himself</b>, addressee of the letter</li><li class=\"d1\">most of what we know comes from <b>these two letters</b></li><li class=\"d1\">will cover as we go through <b>1 and 2 Timothy</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Super brief</b> letters</li><li class=\"d0\">Unlike epistles so far: written to a <b>particular person</b>, not a church or group of churches</li><li class=\"d1\">\"slightly different format\", speaks about <b>slightly different topics</b></li></ul>"},{"t":95.52,"lv":3,"h":"A mentoring letter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Timothy: <b>individual, not a church</b></li><li class=\"d1\">worked closely with Paul</li><li class=\"d1\">holds a <b>leadership position</b> in early Christian communities</li><li class=\"d1\">sent by this letter to fulfill a <b>specific role in church leadership</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not the usual topics: <b>things in particular churches</b>, clarifying theology, practical issues</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul in a <b>mentoring role</b></li><li class=\"d1\">talks to him <b>as a fellow leader</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"here are things you need to keep in mind and look out for\"</li></ul>"},{"t":168.52,"lv":2,"h":"1 Timothy 1:1 - Paul, an apostle","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.1: <b>\"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ, by the commandment of God our Savior and the Lord Jesus Christ our hope\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Typical by now: <b>formal first-century letter</b> elements</li><li class=\"d1\">begins with <b>your name</b> - opposite of English (address first, <b>sign at the bottom</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Apostle</b> = <b>one who is sent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>seeds themes</b> into how he introduces himself at the start of epistles</li><li class=\"d1\">here: sent by Christ <b>on a mission</b></li><li class=\"d1\">this epistle: he is <b>sending Timothy on a mission</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Timothy knows who Paul is - \"he's pointing out with a reason\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God our Savior</b> / <b>Christ our hope</b>: usual <b>doublet</b> of Father and Lord Jesus</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>salvation</b> and <b>future hope</b> = ideas he will develop</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ → God the Father → back to Christ: the <b>Holy Trinity act as one</b></li><li class=\"d1\">three persons, <b>one will, one activity</b> - together in <b>sending Paul</b></li></ul>"},{"t":360.92,"lv":2,"h":"1:2 - A true son in the faith","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.2: <b>\"to Timothy, a true son in the faith, grace, mercy, and peace\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Usual <b>couplet</b> variation; the equivalent of our <b>\"Dear\"</b> - the addressee</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"True son in the faith\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul consistently calls himself a <b>father</b> - to Timothy, whom he mentors, and to people in his churches</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I always point these out\" - <b>Protestant friends don't like that language</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul uses it <b>all the time</b></li><li class=\"d1\">else Paul \"fairly consistently violating\" Christ's <b>Call No Man Father</b> passage → understand Christ differently</li></ul>"},{"t":453.36,"lv":3,"h":"Call no man father","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Christ's words are in a <b>litany of titles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"call no man father\" - one Father in heaven</li><li class=\"d1\">\"call no man teacher\" - one teacher</li><li class=\"d0\">Context: disciples <b>not to seek titles</b> or authority and <b>lord it over</b> those they teach</li><li class=\"d1\">that's how <b>rulers of the Gentiles</b> do it</li><li class=\"d1\">not how disciples lead</li><li class=\"d0\">Targets the titles the <b>Pharisees and rabbis</b> wanted</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>teacher</b> = <i>rabbi</i></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's usage: describes a <b>relationship</b> with particular people</li><li class=\"d1\">not demanding a title <b>out of ego</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"like a son to me, in the faith\" - <b>no domination or control</b> of Timothy</li><li class=\"d0\">A <b>term of affection</b> - \"the opposite\"</li><li class=\"d0\">To churches: \"father\" = <b>he loves them</b>, guides them to <b>maturity</b>, as a father does</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I'm the boss and you're all gonna lick my boots\"</li></ul>"},{"t":575.56,"lv":2,"h":"1:3-5 - Remain in Ephesus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.3-4: <b>\"remain in Ephesus\"</b>, charge some to <b>teach no other doctrine</b>, nor heed <b>fables and endless genealogies</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v.5: purpose of the commandment = <b>love</b> from a <b>pure heart</b>, <b>good conscience</b>, <b>sincere faith</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Timothy often mentioned as Paul's <b>representative</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul can't visit (imprisoned, too far, can't get away) → sends Timothy</li><li class=\"d1\">Timothy returns with a <b>report</b> on issues to be addressed</li><li class=\"d0\">Same situation: Timothy sent to <b>Ephesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>home base</b> of the Christian movement for first couple centuries</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I hope they don't hear this at the Archdiocese\" - everyone says <b>Antioch</b>, really <b>Ephesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul ministered there; <b>St. John</b>, <b>Mary Magdalene</b>, the <b>Theotokos</b> for a while</li><li class=\"d1\">hub city: <b>shipping and commerce</b>, on a <b>main road</b> (cf. Ephesians)</li></ul>"},{"t":703.92,"lv":3,"h":"Fables and genealogies: unimportant disputes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Timothy stays because of <b>issues to resolve</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Differences of opinion</b> on theology that Paul thinks are <b>mostly unimportant</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"this is a <b>heresy</b>, throw them out\"</li><li class=\"d1\">instead: don't listen to <b>fables and endless genealogies</b> = <b>minutiae</b> everyone argues about - \"we still have this today\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Becomes a problem when it makes <b>rifts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">factions, arguing, debating</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>splits the unity of the church</b> → major issue</li></ul>"},{"t":781.88,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: what are the genealogies?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: What about <b>genealogies</b>?</li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>ancestry.com</b> - who descended from whom (why would that matter to pagan converts?)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Religious-world</b> genealogy</li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Hesiod's <i>Theogony</i></b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>systems of thought</b>, <b>rankings of angels</b>, systems of doctrine</li><li class=\"d1\">detailed explanations of <b>planets, stars, constellations</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Big with <b>pagans</b>, who might apply it to Christianity</li><li class=\"d0\">Also big in <b>first-century Judaism</b> - lots of <b>astrology</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Also elaborate <b>symbolism</b> and <b>allegorical interpretations</b> of scripture, then <b>fighting about them</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Taxonomies</b> might be a better translation - \"although even that isn't quite\"</li></ul>"},{"t":902.32,"lv":3,"h":"Why he says drop it: love is the goal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Disputes: <b>nobody advances in the faith</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nobody more <b>pious or virtuous</b> from arguing this</li><li class=\"d1\">\"never had anyone show up at the church and say <b>I lost this argument on the internet</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">v.5 purpose of the commandment: <b>love</b> from pure heart, good conscience, <b>sincere faith</b></li><li class=\"d1\">faith should be more like <b>faithfulness / loyalty</b></li><li class=\"d0\">That is what <b>builds people up</b>, brings <b>community together</b>, brings people <b>closer to Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"this dumb stuff\": <b>who's right, smartest, knows the most</b></li></ul>"},{"t":987.88,"lv":2,"h":"1:6-7 - Strayed into idle talk","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.6-7: some <b>strayed</b> to <b>idle talk</b>, <b>desiring to be teachers of the law</b>, understanding <b>neither what they say nor what they affirm</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Strayed from <b>that kind of love</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now <b>idle talk</b> - want to set themselves up as <b>teachers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm the one in the know and I can explain all this to you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">A problem \"we still have\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>social media</b> made it worse: anyone can decide \"I'm going to be a teacher now\" and build a <b>following</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul had the <b>qualifications</b> to be a teacher of the law, yet says <b>they don't know what they're talking about</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Just making themselves <b>look smart</b>, setting themselves <b>above others</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1079.92,"lv":2,"h":"1:8 - The law is good","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.8: <b>\"the law is good if one uses it lawfully\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"kind of a <b>tautology</b>\" - use the law in accordance with the law</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Law\" = <b><i>Torah</i></b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just <b>moral commandments</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>revelation of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">These people aren't teaching moral do's and don'ts - <b>larger scale</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rephrase: <b>teach Torah on its own terms</b> = what scriptures actually say → <b>good</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1142.24,"lv":2,"h":"1:9-11 - The law is for the lawless","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.9-10: law not for the <b>righteous</b> but for <b>lawless, insubordinate, ungodly, sinners, unholy, profane</b></li><li class=\"d1\">murderers of fathers and mothers, manslayers, fornicators, <b>sodomites</b>, kidnappers, liars, perjurers</li><li class=\"d1\">he leaves out the <b>italicized added words</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v.10-11: anything contrary to <b>sound doctrine</b>, per the <b>glorious gospel of the blessed God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Torah is good but <b>aimed at those who need it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Someone in the church living as a Christian: what matters is <b>love, faithfulness, loyalty</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Teaching Torah is directed to <b>people in Ephesus outside the community</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some listed are <b>euphemistic</b>, some direct</li><li class=\"d1\">\"kidnappers - how many kidnappers were there?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he's talking about <b>people outside the church</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1273.44,"lv":3,"h":"Go outside, don't take over the house","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"You\"</b> here is not Timothy - it's the <b>self-appointed teachers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Want to be a teacher of the law? <b>Go outside</b></li><li class=\"d1\">teach people who <b>don't know Christ</b> about God</li><li class=\"d1\">not set up inside the community → <b>rifts, divisions, arguments</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Doctrine vs. morality</b>: we separate them</li><li class=\"d1\">doctrine = <b>Trinity</b>, <b>two natures of Christ</b>; plus \"moral stuff\"</li><li class=\"d1\">for Paul, these behaviors are <b>against doctrine</b> - <b>no disconnect</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Torah is both</b>: who God and Christ are, and the commandments</li><li class=\"d1\">both called <b>doctrine</b>; <b>gospel includes both</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Want to be a leader? <b>\"Go be a leader\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bring people <b>into</b> the house of God</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"Don't take over the house of God and make it your house\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"Timothy, <b>excommunicate</b> them\" - they're <b>misguided</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if qualified, do the task in the <b>correct place</b>, to the <b>correct audience</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1428.6,"lv":2,"h":"1:12-13 - Paul compares himself","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.12-13: thanks Christ who <b>enabled</b> him, counted him <b>faithful</b>, put him into the <b>ministry</b></li><li class=\"d1\">formerly <b>blasphemer, persecutor, insolent man</b></li><li class=\"d1\">obtained <b>mercy</b> because he acted <b>ignorantly in unbelief</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Comparing <b>these people to himself</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He <b>didn't know Christ</b>, didn't really know God - \"thought he did\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Yet God <b>counted him faithful</b> and brought him into ministry</li><li class=\"d0\">Can happen for these people</li><li class=\"d1\">now <b>ignorant</b>, causing problems</li><li class=\"d1\">Timothy can <b>redirect their energies</b> to help the <b>ministry of the Lord</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1515.36,"lv":2,"h":"1:14-17 - Chief of sinners","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.14-15: grace <b>exceedingly abundant</b>; <b>faithful saying</b>: Christ came to save sinners, <b>\"of whom I am chief\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">The prayer <b>before communion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">we pray it about <b>ourselves</b>, not \"of whom St. Paul is chief\"</li><li class=\"d1\">ought to <b>actually mean it</b> - \"easy to say but hard to mean\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the back-of-head thought: \"I know this guy who's probably the chief, but I'm pretty bad too\" → <b>\"not the point\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's point: <b>if he can save me, he can save these people too</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm as bad as it gets\" → <b>mercy available to everybody</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if anyone couldn't find salvation, \"I'm in deep trouble\"</li><li class=\"d0\">v.16-17: mercy so that in him <b>first</b> Christ shows all <b>long suffering</b> as a <b>pattern</b> to those who will believe</li><li class=\"d1\">doxology: <b>king eternal, immortal, invisible, God who alone is wise</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul = a <b>pattern</b>; others can find salvation <b>the same way</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1663.88,"lv":2,"h":"1:18-20 - The charge and the prophecies","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v.18-20: charge to Timothy per <b>prophecies previously made</b>, to <b>wage the good warfare</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"why couldn't they just say <b>fight the good fight</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">some rejected <b>faith and good conscience</b>, <b>suffered shipwreck</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Hymenaeus and Alexander</b>, <b>delivered to Satan</b> to learn not to blaspheme</li><li class=\"d0\">\"I'm charging you with this\" - because of prophecies concerning him</li><li class=\"d1\">not weird predictions or <b>signs in the sky at his birth</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1743.12,"lv":3,"h":"What prophecy means","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">From <b>1 Corinthians</b>: prophecy = <b>speaking and revealing the things of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses</b> = first and main prophet, the <b>paradigm</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a couple of predictions, but \"<b>.1%</b>\" predicting the future</li><li class=\"d1\">mostly <b>teaching and preaching</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Deuteronomy</b> = a long <b>sermon</b> before Canaan</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nathan</b> and David: not predicting - telling about the <b>past</b>, convicting him</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Isaiah, Jeremiah, Ezekiel</b>: convict the people of sin</li><li class=\"d0\">Line between prophecy and <b>preaching</b> = \"very slender\", sometimes <b>non-existent</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: you've heard me, and <b>other apostles</b> - <b>we all commissioned you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">keep acting on what has been <b>preached and proclaimed</b> for you</li></ul>"},{"t":1836.04,"lv":3,"h":"Good warfare and shipwreck","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Good warfare</b> = <b>spiritual warfare</b>, not picking fights</li><li class=\"d1\">he just said the <b>opposite</b> of picking fights in the church</li><li class=\"d0\">Others also <b>rejected that preaching and teaching</b> - he names a couple</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Shipwreck</b> imagery</li><li class=\"d1\">out at sea with a <b>course</b>; stray → <b>trouble</b> \"in a thousand ways\"</li><li class=\"d1\">the preaching = the <b>course</b>; usually <b>way and road</b> language, this is <b>sea lane</b> language</li><li class=\"d1\">they ignored the <b>course instructions</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Notice: <b>shipwrecked</b>, not \"terrible people\" or \"we hate them\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they're <b>in trouble, need help</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul was <b>shipwrecked twice</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1934.08,"lv":3,"h":"Delivered to Satan","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two examples, <b>delivered to Satan</b> to learn not to blaspheme</li><li class=\"d0\">Same language in <b>1 Corinthians</b>: handed over for <b>destruction of the flesh</b> that the soul be saved - \"even more drastic\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Demonic powers</b>: why does God let them <b>roam causing trouble</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">they want evil, to <b>destroy humans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">yet God uses them to <b>test and try</b> people → <b>repentance and faith</b>, \"against their wills\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"begrudgingly they end up <b>serving him</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">So handed over <b>not to go to hell</b> but to <b>learn not to blaspheme</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2020.68,"lv":3,"h":"God's wrath: no longer protecting","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Paradigmatic</b> for much of the OT and a fair amount of the NT</li><li class=\"d0\">God's <b>wrath and punishing</b> = God <b>no longer protecting</b> people from the <b>consequences of their actions</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Only reason Satan doesn't have everyone: <b>God stopping him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">me vs. the devil, I <b>lose every time</b>: \"vast cosmic intelligence, I'm a dude\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"God disciplines every son whom he loves\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">discipline a child not from hate or anger - to <b>get them back in line</b>, keep from something worse</li><li class=\"d1\">kid playing in the street, <b>swat on the rear</b> → goal: not hit by a <b>truck</b>, not an arbitrary rule</li><li class=\"d0\">Handing over = <b>excommunicate</b></li><li class=\"d1\">outside the church, in the part of the world <b>under Satan's control</b> - \"not going to be fun\"</li><li class=\"d1\">hope: he <b>repents</b>, \"fix what I broke\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2172.72,"lv":3,"h":"Letting them feel consequences","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Sometimes you <b>let the leash go a little</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Child never experiences <b>consequences</b>, always shielded → \"a <b>monster</b>, rather literally\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>immoral narcissistic</b> monster</li><li class=\"d0\">Loving parent wants an <b>adult who's a human</b> → let them experience <b>a little</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not the <b>truck</b></li><li class=\"d1\">earn the money to <b>pay for the window they broke</b></li><li class=\"d0\">No desire for these people to be <b>tormented by Satan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but if it's the only thing that might bring <b>repentance</b> → <b>let it happen</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2265.56,"lv":2,"h":"Chapter 1 through-line: troublemakers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Whole chapter: Paul to Timothy about <b>troublemakers in Ephesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a couple of <b>serious ones, excommunicated</b></li><li class=\"d1\">a bunch of <b>lower-grade ones</b> active in the community</li><li class=\"d1\">may <b>change day to day</b> - some get their act together, others start trouble</li><li class=\"d0\">Question: <b>\"How do you handle the troublemakers?\"</b> - as a <b>fellow leader</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Through line: Paul's concern is their <b>coming to Christ</b> - wants their <b>repentance</b></li><li class=\"d1\">low-grade: <b>redirect and use it for the gospel</b>, get them <b>back on board</b></li><li class=\"d1\">serious (the two): <b>blaspheming</b> - but Paul was a <b>blasphemer</b> before conversion → <b>hope</b>; more <b>drastic action</b> to bring them back</li><li class=\"d1\">even <b>pagans in Ephesus</b> outside: Paul wants <b>all</b> to know Christ and be saved</li><li class=\"d0\">Strategizing with Timothy: <b>mentor to protege, father to son</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"figure out what <b>approach</b> for different people, but the <b>goal's the same</b>\"</li></ul>"}]});
